# Headline replay-fixture identity - SHA-256 (GAP-0002 / GAP-0040).
#
# These are the LOCAL-ONLY, NON-COMMITTABLE inputs the committed replay tools and
# headline experiments load (save states, the pristine disc, the from-boot movie).
# Per the Preservation Policy we record the *hash* (committable, identity-pinning)
# but NEVER the bytes. This is the "hash-pinned" half of the GAP-0002 acceptance
# bar ("every fixture is regenerable or hash-pinned").
#
# ADVISORY contract (distinct from tools/repro_inputs.sha256, which fails-if-missing):
#   - A fixture absent on this host is fine (clean clone / fresh machine) -> never fails.
#   - A fixture PRESENT but with a different hash is fixture drift -> flagged.
#   tools/verify_repro_inputs.py keeps the fail-if-missing CORE manifest; this file is
#   parsed + verified by tests/test_fixtures_manifest.py (skip-if-absent).
#
# Format (3 fields; path may contain spaces -> split on first two whitespace runs):
#   <sha256>  <role>  <path-or-env-pattern>
# Path conventions match the replay tools: $ABL_SAVESTATES defaults to
# ~/.local/share/duckstation/savestates; bare names are repo-root-relative.
# Verify one by hand:  sha256sum "$ABL_SAVESTATES/SCUS-94288_g30_openground.sav"
# Computed locally 2026-06-21 from the owner's inputs (game_serial SCUS-94288, USA V1.0).
#
# RETIRED 2026-07-08: the numbered-SLOT states SCUS-94288_1/_2/_3.sav
# (roles spawn-floor-level01 / fixture-scus2 / level02-scene3-default) are no
# longer pinned -- numbered quick-save slots get overwritten by normal play and
# had drifted. Named save states are the only supported fixture class; replay
# tools now take an explicit --save (see also ABL_SPAWN_SAV for the live test).
#
# The preserved DuckStation fork + clean-built binary identity (GAP-0001) is pinned
# separately in tools/FORK_COMMIT.txt (fork 296955321; clean binary fd4bf9ed...);
# not duplicated here.

